  "chain": "hardened graphite grease [cause TBD] -> RTB cell switch incorrectly signals racked-out position -> spurious backup turbine trip relay actuation -> automatic reactor trip [AFW auto-initiated] -> (parallel) SV-3-1440 air leak -> CV-3-2830 slow to close -> RCS cooldown/pressurizer level drop/letdown auto-isolation",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Official cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields, despite narrative identifying a fairly specific proximate mechanism (hardened lubricant/electrical tracking) and a PM-program weakness (condition-based rather than prescriptive procedure). Two independent failure chains occurred concurrently: (1) RTB cell switch malfunction causing the trip itself, and (2) an unrelated SDTC valve solenoid air leak causing sluggish valve closure after the trip; both are modeled as parallel/sequential FailureModes feeding into related but distinct Consequences. No explicit backup system is stated as compensating for the RTB/cell-switch failure itself (the trip breakers are protective devices, not backed up); AFW is noted only as the expected/automatic post-trip response, not a backup to a failure, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was asserted for it. SIMILAR EVENTS section states no similar prior events were found -- no stub LER created."
